From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zahary@metacraft-labs.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add a MacOS OSType constant
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`OSType` has constants for Windows and Linux only, so every caller that
wants to talk about a macOS guest has to spell `params.OSType("macos")`
inline. External providers already do exactly that — a provider driving
Apple Virtualization guests has no other way to say what it is running —
and the string is what garm stores, what it exports as the `os_type`
metrics label, and what it hands back in `BootstrapInstance`.

Name it once, so that garm and the providers agree on the spelling and so
that the OS allow-lists in garm can refer to it by constant.

This adds a name; it does not make any existing code path treat macOS
differently. In particular `util.GetTools()` and `cloudconfig` still
accept only Linux and Windows — a provider that renders its own runner
bootstrap (as the Apple-silicon ones do) does not reach them, and
widening them is a separate change with its own testing story.

Signed-off-by: Zahary Karadjov <zahary@metacraft-labs.com>
---
 params/params.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/params/params.go b/params/params.go
index a4e5529..83e40b6 100644
--- a/params/params.go
+++ b/params/params.go
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ type (
 const (
 	Windows OSType = "windows"
 	Linux   OSType = "linux"
+	MacOS   OSType = "macos"
 	Unknown OSType = "unknown"
 )
 
--
2.51.0
